{"record":"parent_entry","position":{"parent_record":"request:00000000000000000019:0000","subposition":null},"original_role":"tool","source":"tool_result","trust":"untrusted","provenance":null,"content":"{\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"call_id\":\"call_01a1654af1ca71f589194b208651964a\",\"output\":\"Read text file `SECURITY_REVIEW.md`.\\n1|# Security Review (2026-05-04)\\n2|\\n3|## Findings\\n4|\\n5|### 1) Unvalidated persistent deserialization from `localStorage` allows persistent state corruption / DoS-by-data\\n6|- **Where:** `game.js` `loadMetaProgress()` and `loadBestRun()` parse attacker-controlled `localStorage` and trust fields with no type/range checks.\\n7|- **Impact:** Any script running on the same origin (including browser extensions, compromised third-party scripts on the same host, or a user self-modifying state) can persist malformed values (e.g., strings, negative numbers, extreme values, objects) that break game invariants, produce `NaN` math propagation, or soft-lock logic across sessions.\\n8|- **Why this is a security issue:** This is insecure deserialization of untrusted persistent data in the browser context. While it does not enable RCE here, it enables persistent integrity loss and denial-of-service behavior.\\n9|- **Fix:** Validate parsed objects with a strict schema (numeric fields only, bounded ranges, defaults on invalid), and reject unknown keys before merging.\\n10|\\n11|### 2) GPL-3.0 distribution compliance risk: third-party asset provenance not documented\\n12|- **Where:** `assets/` contains numerous image files, but repository documentation does not provide per-asset license/provenance metadata.\\n13|- **Impact:** If any asset is sourced under non-GPL-compatible terms (or without redistribution rights), open-source distribution can violate copyright terms despite GPL-3.0 code licensing.\\n14|- **Why this is a security/compliance issue:** Licensing non-compliance is a legal supply-chain risk that can force takedowns or re-licensing.\\n15|- **Fix:** Add an `ASSETS_LICENSES.md` (or SPDX manifest) listing each asset, source URL/author, exact license, and compatibility status.\\n16|\\n17|## Scope checks completed\\n18|- Command injection: no shell/process execution paths found.\\n19|- Path traversal: no filesystem path handling APIs used.\\n20|- Hardcoded secrets: none found.\\n21|- Unsafe dependencies: no package manager / external runtime dependencies present in-repo.\\n22|- Race conditions & info-leaking error handling: no server-side concurrency surfaces; no sensitive exception disclosure observed.\"}","truncated":false}
